### UC04 – Change Participants (happy path)
# Prerequisite: first create a booking with UC01 and copy the returned bookingId below.
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookings/{{bookingId}}/participants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "newParticipantCount": 5
}

### UC04 – Error: booking not found (404)
# A random UUID that does not exist in the system.
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookings/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/participants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "newParticipantCount": 5
}

### UC04 – Error: invalid state transition (409)
# Prerequisite: cancel a booking first (UC03), then attempt to change participants.
# Attempting to change participants on a CANCELLED (or ACTIVE/COMPLETED) booking triggers InvalidBookingStateException.
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookings/{{bookingId}}/participants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "newParticipantCount": 5
}

### UC04 – Error: capacity exceeded (409)
# NOT REPRODUCIBLE LOCALLY. CapacityExceededException maps to 409, but
# StubAvailabilityChecker returns AvailableCapacity(Integer.MAX_VALUE), so no
# newParticipantCount can exceed it and this request returns 200.
# (An earlier comment here claimed the stub returns 50. It does not, and never did.)
# To exercise it, bind an AvailabilityChecker with finite capacity in
# bootstrap/BookingConfig. Covered by
# TourBookingTest.changeParticipants_exceedingCapacity_throwsCapacityExceededException,
# ChangeParticipantsDriverTest.change_throwsCapacityExceededException_whenNewCountExceedsCapacity
# and TourBookingControllerTest.changeParticipants_returns409_whenCapacityExceeded.
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookings/{{bookingId}}/participants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "newParticipantCount": 999
}

### UC04 – Validation error: newParticipantCount below minimum (400)
# @Min(1) on ChangeParticipantsRequest rejects this at the HTTP boundary.
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookings/{{bookingId}}/participants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "newParticipantCount": 0
}

### UC04 – Error: availability check failure (502)
# NOT REPRODUCIBLE LOCALLY. AvailabilityUnavailableException maps to 502, but the
# local StubAvailabilityChecker never fails, so this request returns 200.
# To exercise it, replace the StubAvailabilityChecker binding in
# bootstrap/BookingConfig with an implementation that throws
# AvailabilityUnavailableException. Covered by
# ChangeParticipantsDriverTest.change_propagatesAvailabilityUnavailableException.
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookings/{{bookingId}}/participants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "newParticipantCount": 5
}
